80
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:46,940
God saw the light and the light was good.

81
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:48,900
And he separated the light from the darkness.

82
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:52,420
God called the light day and the darkness, he called night.

83
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:56,960
And there was evening and there was morning the first day.

84
00:04:56,960 --> 00:05:03,180
And every day of creation goes on like this, that God creates and then he says it's good.

85
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:06,040
And then there's evening and morning the next day.

86
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,340
God creates the light.

87
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,640
He says, it's good.

88
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,600
There's evening and morning.

89
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,540
He creates land and sea and he says it's good.

90
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:13,740
And there's evening and there's morning.

91
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:17,460
He creates plants on the surface of the earth and he calls them good.

92
00:05:17,460 --> 00:05:18,580
And there's evening and morning.

93
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:22,380
He creates lights in the sky, the sun and the stars and the moon.

94
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:24,060
He says that they're good.

95
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,780
There's evening and morning.

96
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:28,600
He creates fish and birds and he blesses them.

97
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:31,340
And he goes, he says, fill up the sea and fill up the sky.

98
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:32,620
And he says, you're good.

99
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:34,480
And there's evening and morning.

100
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:39,300
He creates creatures on the land and humans and he blesses them.

101
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:40,340
And he says, fill it up.

102
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,680
And he says, you're good.

103
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,140
And there's evening and morning.

104
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:44,720
There's this rhythm God creates.

105
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,160
He says, it's good.

106
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:46,940
There's evening.

107
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,260
And then there's morning.

108
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:54,580
And then we get to verse 31 and it says this, God saw all that he had made and it was very

109
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:54,880
good.

110
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,240
The Hebrew there is tov mayod.

111
00:05:56,240 --> 00:06:03,360
They don't have the idea of necessarily perfection like we have it, but it's this idea that nature

112
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:08,600
is complete, that the world that he has created has everything that it needs to keep going.

113
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,280
There's nothing that it's missing.

114
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:13,020
And he said, it's very good.

115
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:13,920
It's tov mayod.

116
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:17,200
God saw all that he made and it was very good.

117
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:21,100
And there was evening and there was morning, the sixth day, thus the heavens and the earth

118
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:23,000
were completed in all their vast array.

119
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,920
And by the seventh day, God had finished the work that he'd been doing.

120
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:33,400
So on the seventh day, he rested from all of his work and God blessed the seventh day and

121
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:38,440
made it holy because on it, he rested from the work of creating that he had done.

122
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:42,180
And this is our first look at Sabbath, right?

123
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:49,240
God works and he says it's good and then he rests.

124
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:53,320
And later on in the story, we're told that we're created in the image of this God.

125
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:56,600
And what we know of God to this point is this rhythm, right?

126
00:06:56,600 --> 00:07:00,720
He creates, he says it's good and he rests.

127
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:09,240
And obviously later on in the story, sin enters the world and this spirals and the pain and sin

128
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,640
is introduced into the world.

129
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:16,460
But even when God decides to wipe it clean through a flood, he preserves his goodness and

130
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:18,720
the ark with Noah and the animals.

131
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:24,220
And when he lands them safely, he puts this good back into the world and he says, fill it up,

132
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:24,760
